e's saying his wife did it  that's going to work against him so  those are two of the strongest points i  think the prosecution is going to use  against him in this horrific case and  just the scene itself i think is going  to offend that jury  all right phillip you've already proven  to us you can lose the defense and still  keep going strong so let's let me ask  you this question  tote may be told two or three different  stories so what facts do you think the  defense will focus on in their opening  statement to try to raise reasonable  doubt  well first of all i'm going to hope that  they're going to wear a sharp kenneth  cole suit with a kenneth cole briefcase  it's a bruno molly shoes because you  want to divert the jury's attention away  from the evidence but having said that  uh if  they can get another pre-trial ruling  that one of those confessions  despite it being unmirandized was in  fact involuntary it is inadmissible even  for impeachment purposes so that if he  decides to take the stand he cannot be  impeached with any prior statement that  he gave during that interrogation now  having said that he's still going to  have to deal with the other statement  and he could always argue that he was  still defending his wife in other words  he was covering for her and he did it to  the bitter end but he finally threw in  the towel when he realized that nobody  was coming to his rescue all right  interesting defense we'll see if it can  uh pan out of course we're keeping eyes  on in this case as it starts up on  monday when we come back it's johnny  depp versus amber hur the highly  anticipated trial of the hollywood stars  and exes is set to begin on monday what  you can expect from the defamation  lawsuit next  welcome back we're getting a closer look  into the lives of hollywood's elites as  part of the defamation lawsuit between  a-lister johnny depp and ex-wife amber  hurd here's what we've got so far depp  is suing heard in a 50 million dollar  defamation suit based on a washington  post op-ed written by herd the article  was published back in 2018 entitled  quote i spoke up against sexual violence  and face our culture's wrath that has to  change in the article heard details  being exposed to abuse at a young age  and how she quote had the rare vantage  point of seeing in real time how  institutions protect men accused of  abuse depp alleges heard's article  caused him to lose work including a  starring role in yet another pirates of  the caribbean film in response to the  suit hurt filed a hundred million dollar  counter claim depp is expected to  testify in the case and maybe even other  celebrities including james franco elon  musk and paul bettany testimony will  likely surround the alleged abuse  stemming from the couple's relationship  between 2015 and 2016. depp says heard  abused him she argues he physically  emotionally and verbally abuse her on  several occasions audio recordings give  us a glimpse into the pair's short-lived  romance  we've got to change how we do things and  i want to trust you and i feel like all  the trust is gone all the trust is gone  in the relationship because you keep  splitting  i'm not gonna be in a physical  altercation with you  then don't you  hit me last night  what about all the other times you split  come on you cannot act like that it's  about that it's on a plane i can't split  no and you hit back so don't act like  you don't participate i pushed you  i'm not gonna get into the details of  that fight you and i both know that you  split when there is no physical violence  involved  and that you do it and meet like at the  very beginning of fights these days and  if you split and you go into a different  room and you don't actually leave that  house it does nothing but perpetuate the  fight  really when you split on me how do you  feel when i leave you well i live when i  go into the other room  and giving me a room i mean getting  another room in a hotel is just the same  thing  when did i get another room and  hopefully you uh text steven or nathan  in toronto to get you into the room  let's bring back la county deputy public  defender philip dube and co-host terry  austin one last time as we look ahead to  what seems will be a blockbuster  defamation trial phillip depp is  expected to testify and some pretty big  names like elon musk and the others we  mentioned but if they aren't in the same  jurisdiction of the court will they  likely be forced to testify  oh absolutely uh we have uh in the  united states there is a uniform statute  it's called the uniform act to secure  attendance of witnesses from without the  state and what you do is in your home  jurisdiction you petition your judge  for an order to be served on the  jurisdiction where the necessary witness  resides you make out a showing of  materiality and necessity for the  testimony and it gets served on the  other jurisdiction and a judge in a  dedicated courtroom rules on whether or  not they will open a case and issue  subpoenas ordering them to appear in the  jurisdiction where trial is pending it's  a very common procedure especially in  criminal cases yeah i just want to see  elon musk come in as a hologram and  testify that way that's going to make me  happy but terry what's on the line for  herd in depth in this case and who has  to prove what exactly to win  listen he's claiming defamation and he's  basically saying that her statements  about him were false that she knowingly  made those statements that she  maliciously made those statements and  he's got to prove that it damaged his  reputation frankly i think he will be  able to do that we know he lost some  movie deals because of it on that  pirates franchise and so i think he  could possibly win all right we'll see  how this goes of course law and crime  will be there covering the case thank  you for joining us here at law and crime  daily we'll see you next time as we  discuss justice in america  [Music] 